{"metadata":{"title":"Schedule","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L100","fileName":"Schedule.swift"}},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","generated":true,"title":"Building and Running Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A schedule holds the systems of one frame or step of a simulation. You build it by listing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the systems in a closure, and run it on a world with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which runs each system once:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 2, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 4.0, y: 70.0)\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Ordering-Systems","text":"Ordering Systems"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or before one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written earlier, by ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its written place:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to throw","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","text":"Running Systems at the Same Time"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two systems ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"conflict"}]},{"text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time. The world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order, except that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on how they happen to be written. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},{"type":"text","text":" lists those pairs, so a test can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keep a schedule free of them."}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Creating-a-Schedule","title":"Creating a Schedule","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/